.TH DDN-FETCH "1" "2026\-11\-25" "ddnetmirror 0.0.1" "ddnetmirror manual"
.SH NAME
ddn fetch \- fetch running configs, LLDP links and a Containerlab topology from CloudVision
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ddn
fetch [-h] --server SERVER (--hostname HOSTNAME | --tag EXPR) [--exclude-host HOSTNAME] [--list] [--ca-file CA_FILE] [--token-file PATH] [--output OUTPUT | --output-dir OUTPUT_DIR] [--lldp] [--lab-name LAB_NAME] [--image IMAGE] [--fixup-rules RULES.yml] [--verbose] [--force]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Fetch running configs from CloudVision and save them unchanged. Only EOS devices are selected: those with CloudVision's system\-generated eos tag. The service\-account token is read from \-\-token\-file, else from CLOUDVISION_TOKEN, else from $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ddnetmirror/token (default ~/.config/ddnetmirror/token).

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-server\fR \fI\,SERVER\/\fR
CloudVision host[:port] (default port 443)

.TP
\fB\-\-hostname\fR \fI\,HOSTNAME\/\fR
device hostname as shown in CloudVision inventory (any case)

.TP
\fB\-\-tag\fR \fI\,EXPR\/\fR
device tag KEY=VALUE (exact, case\-sensitive), a bare KEY (the tag with any
value), or an expression of such terms with not, and, or (in that precedence)
and parentheses, e.g. '(site=lab or site=dr) and not role=spine' or 'site=lab
and not role'; 'not' covers EOS devices without the tag. and, or, not are
reserved words. Must match exactly one device unless \-\-output\-dir or \-\-list is
given

.TP
\fB\-\-exclude\-host\fR \fI\,HOSTNAME\/\fR
with \-\-tag: leave out the selected device with this inventory hostname (exact,
any case) before anything is collected; repeat for more devices. A hostname
matching no selected device is a warning

.TP
\fB\-\-list\fR
print the devices \-\-hostname or \-\-tag selects (hostname, serial, EOS version)
and stop: no configs are fetched and no files are written. \-\-tag may match
many devices

.TP
\fB\-\-ca\-file\fR \fI\,CA_FILE\/\fR
PEM CA bundle for on\-prem CVP with a private CA

.TP
\fB\-\-token\-file\fR \fI\,PATH\/\fR
read the CloudVision token from this file instead of CLOUDVISION_TOKEN or the
default token file (e.g. one file per environment). Same checks as the default
file: owner\-only regular file, not a symlink; an unusable file is an error

.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI\,OUTPUT\/\fR
output file (default: <device hostname>.cfg); never overwritten

.TP
\fB\-\-output\-dir\fR \fI\,OUTPUT_DIR\/\fR
with \-\-tag: collect every device with the tag into DIR/configs/original as
<hostname>.cfg, unchanged

.TP
\fB\-\-lldp\fR
with \-\-output\-dir: also report LLDP links between the collected devices

.TP
\fB\-\-lab\-name\fR \fI\,LAB_NAME\/\fR
with \-\-lldp: also write a Containerlab topology DIR/<NAME>.clab.yml

.TP
\fB\-\-image\fR \fI\,IMAGE\/\fR
with \-\-lab\-name: cEOS image for every topology node, no Docker check. Without
it, a local ceos:VERSION image is picked per device by EOS version (needs
Docker; version matching only, not a compatibility check)

.TP
\fB\-\-fixup\-rules\fR \fI\,RULES.yml\/\fR
with \-\-lab\-name: write copies of the collected configs transformed by these
rules to DIR/configs/lab, and use those as startup configs. Default:
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ddnetmirror/fixups.yml (~/.config/ddnetmirror/fixups.yml) if
it exists; 'none' disables fixups

.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
with \-\-lab\-name and fixup rules: print what each rule changed per device;
never prints config text

.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
with \-\-output\-dir: replace existing generated files (original and lab configs,
topology) instead of refusing; no backups, other files untouched

.SH DISTRIBUTION
The latest version of ddnetmirror may be downloaded from
.UR https://github.com/DaphnisDuck/ddnetmirror
.UE
